# ERCOT CRR Market Analytics -- backend environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (or set these as real environment variables /
# secrets in whatever process manager runs this backend) and fill in the
# values that apply. Nothing here is required -- with nothing set, the
# backend runs fine against the built-in synthetic demo dataset.
#
# Load order for the main dataset (Dashboard / Participants / Opportunity
# Signals): SQL Server (below) -> CSV files in data/raw/ -> synthetic demo.
# The first one that's configured AND reachable wins. See backend/app/db.py
# and backend/app/ingestion.py for full details.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTION A: SQL Server -- one connection string
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you already have a full SQLAlchemy connection string, set just this one
# variable and skip Option B entirely.
#
# DATABASE_URL=mssql+pyodbc://USERNAME:PASSWORD@HOST:1433/DATABASE_NAME?driver=ODBC+Driver+18+for+SQL+Server


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTION B: SQL Server -- separate pieces (used if DATABASE_URL is not set)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SQL_SERVER_HOST=your-server-hostname-or-ip
# SQL_SERVER_PORT=1433
# SQL_SERVER_DATABASE=ERCOT_CRR
# SQL_SERVER_TABLE=crr_auction_records
# SQL_SERVER_DRIVER=ODBC Driver 18 for SQL Server
# SQL_SERVER_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=10
#
# Then EITHER SQL authentication:
# SQL_SERVER_USERNAME=your_username
# SQL_SERVER_PASSWORD=your_password
#
# OR Windows/trusted-connection authentication (no username/password, Windows only):
# SQL_SERVER_TRUSTED_CONNECTION=yes


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real ERCOT auction CSVs (used only if SQL Server above is not configured)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Drop ERCOT CRR Auction Result CSVs (NP7-802-M / NP7-803-M layout) into
# data/raw/ -- no environment variable needed, they're picked up automatically.
# Override the data directory itself if needed:
# CRR_DATA_DIR=/path/to/data


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ERCOT's live Public Data API (separate capability -- real-time DAM price
# spread and binding-constraint data, NOT auction/participant data; see
# ercot_live.py's module docstring). Free registration at
# https://apiexplorer.ercot.com/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ERCOT_API_USERNAME=you@example.com
# ERCOT_API_PASSWORD=your-apiexplorer-password
# ERCOT_API_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY=your-subscription-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verifying your configuration once the backend is running
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GET /health               -- is the process up (always fast, no DB touch)
# GET /api/system/status    -- which data source is ACTUALLY active right
#                               now, whether SQL is configured, and any
#                               warning if SQL was configured but couldn't
#                               be used (falls back to CSV/synthetic and
#                               says so rather than failing silently)
# GET /api/live/status      -- whether the ERCOT live API credentials above
#                               are configured
